
arlo -- RAM-backed Debian arm64 initramfs (iPhone SE 1st gen / A9 s8003 / n69ap)

What works here:  a shell, coreutils, dpkg, busybox -- all from RAM.
What does not:    storage, USB host, Wi-Fi, network, PMIC (power/battery/RTC),
                  GPU, and the camera. None of those drivers exist upstream
                  for A9. There is no disk to install to and no way to save
                  anything. Rebooting loses everything, by design.

If you can read this on the phone's screen, the framebuffer console is up --
that is a much bigger result than the shell itself.

Full statement: /etc/arlo/CAPABILITY.txt
